  resolution: 'Harold Benn\'s lip was perfectly well. He walked behind the vicarage tent with his cornet case while his band played without him, lifted the tin from the trestle the verger had abandoned for the coconut shy, and put it where a cornet should go. The verger lied about his post, and Nancy Lund lied about hers for a reason with a spaniel. The tin was in the cornet case; the cornet was in the ditch behind the bier house.',
